# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b2), edited. baltus_tolliver's first conversation.

~ start
set baltus_tolliver_met
Narrator: Sweet pipe smoke and oiled leather hang warm in the rafters of the post. Behind the counter, a slender man in spotless grey studies you with dark, practiced eyes.
baltus_tolliver [smile]: Step in out of the damp, friends. If it exists in Druskenvald, it passes through Tolliver's Trading Post sooner or later, and if it does not, I know who carries it.
* Browse their wares -> shop_open
* Ask how a city merchant ended up on this moor -> about_self
* Ask what he makes of Wickermoor Village -> about_village
* Ask after any strange goods passing through -> rumour
* [Perception DC 14] Study his rings and the carved mahogany pipe -> pipe_ok | pipe_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ menu
baltus_tolliver [neutral]: Take your time, friends. Everything has a price, and I am a reasonable man.
* Browse their wares -> shop_open
* Ask how a city merchant ended up on this moor -> about_self
* Ask what he makes of Wickermoor Village -> about_village
* Ask after any strange goods passing through -> rumour
* [Perception DC 14] Study his rings and the carved mahogany pipe -> pipe_ok | pipe_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ shop_open
baltus_tolliver [smile]: Have a look at the shelves, and tell me if your tastes run rarer.
shop
-> menu

~ about_self
baltus_tolliver [sly]: A man goes where he is needed, and the moor had a sharp need for civilised commerce. Besides, the air out here has been waking up lately.
-> menu

~ about_village
baltus_tolliver [neutral]: Mayor Somerton keeps his flock singing to oaks and stones, and they pay their bills on time. Keep your blades sheathed indoors and we will get along splendidly.
-> menu

~ rumour
baltus_tolliver [sly]: If you fancy odd machinery, there is a riverboat engine down on the water built by another Stranger like yourselves. Folks pay good coin for parts from the old world.
-> menu

~ pipe_ok
set cult_clue_baltus_tolliver
Narrator: Where his silver ring taps the mahogany bowl, a leaping hare is worked into the dark grain, and tiny antlers are stamped inside the band.
baltus_tolliver [smile]: You have a sharp eye for small work. An old family token from the deep woods, nothing I keep on the shelves for sale.
-> menu

~ pipe_fail
Narrator: A curl of spiced smoke drifts between you, and he slips the mahogany pipe neatly into his pocket.
baltus_tolliver [smile]: Careful staring too long at a merchant's hands, friend, or I will think you are pricing my rings.
-> menu
